Hmm — scope check: is this worth fixing now? It's a genuine a11y polish item (H-23 / keyboard accessibility): after undo via keyboard, focus drops to body; subsequent Tab restarts from top. Fix: after render, restore focus to an equivalent control. Implement: before re-render, remember activeElement identity (data-act+data-dim or id), after innerHTML, find matching element and focus({preventScroll:true}). Central in render()? Store in render() entry: capture attrs; after all renderers, restore. Legend items also rebuilt (they carry data-act=legend data-val). Chips rebuilt. Buttons rebuilt with same data-act/data-dim → restore via selector `[data-act="..."][data-dim="..."]` or for legend `[data-act="legend"][data-val="..."]`, rail `.dim-name[data-dim]`, buttons `#btn-undo` etc.

